        "instruction": {
          "title": "Inspect the double helix components",
          "description": "Examine the two sugar-phosphate backbones spiraling around a common axis. Then look inward to the nitrogenous bases. Identify adenine, thymine, guanine, and cytosine, and note that the bases pair across the helix through hydrogen bonds."
